Newsreader and Public Sans are both licensed under the SIL Open Font License,
Version 1.1, which permits bundling them with this software.

  Newsreader   — Production Type, https://fonts.google.com/specimen/Newsreader
  Public Sans  — USWDS,           https://fonts.google.com/specimen/Public+Sans

Both files here are the latin subset of the variable font, taken from Google
Fonts, and they are the same two files the web panel carries — the docs and the
panel are one product and are set in one pair of faces.

They are served from this origin rather than fetched from a font host, for the
same reason the site has no analytics and no CDN: the whole page is what is
shipped, and a documentation site that stops rendering correctly because a third
party is unreachable is a documentation site nobody can rely on offline.

The full licence text travels with each family upstream:
https://openfontlicense.org
